==English==
{{wikipedia|decipherment|lang=en}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|decypher}}

===Etymology===
As {{m|en|decypher}}, but not retaining the {{m|en||y}} from the {{cog|fro|-}} [[etymon|etyma]] of {{m|en|cipher}} ({{m|fro|cyfre}}, {{m|fro|cyffre}}); the {{m|en||i}} spelling tends to be preferred etymologically, being consistent with its [[cognate]]s, the {{cog|fr|déchiffrer}} and the {{cog|it|decifrare}}, and with their common ancestor, the {{cog|ML.|cifra}}, {{m|la|cifera}}, {{m|la|ciphra}}. {{surf|en|de-|cipher}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/dɪˈsaɪfə(ɹ)/|a=UK}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-decipher.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|aɪfə(ɹ)|s=3}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[convert]] a [[code]] or [[cipher]] to plain [[text]].
#: {{syn|en|decode|decrypt|uncode<qq:rare>}}
#: {{ant|en|encipher|encode|encrypt}}
#: {{cot|en|recipher|recode}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[read]] text that is almost [[illegible]] or [[obscure]]
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[make sense of]] a complex [[situation]].
#* {{RQ:Landon Francesca Carrara|page=13|volume=II|text=Truly, we need human infirmity to teach us human nature, and that to Louis had been as a sealed book; he had only seen the coloured and gilded outside: too late he had to '''decipher''' the rough and gloomy page within.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To find a [[solution]] to a [[problem]].

